# DEBT-0024 — Traceability Broken by Uncommitted PAEOS-9 Execution Architecture Dependency

Status: **OPEN** · Filed: 2026-08-06 · Channel: CER-3
Level: **specifications & traceability** (touches `spec/SAEOS-1-architecture.md` §1.1).
Source: Mission 0 Census Audit (`SAEOS-1` §1.1).

## 1. Observation

`spec/SAEOS-1-architecture.md` (§1.1 and §11 Traceability) heavily cites `spec/PAEOS-9-execution-architecture.md` for consumption contracts, emission schemas, and non-authority guarantees (§10 of PAEOS-9).

However, on `origin/main`, `spec/PAEOS-9-execution-architecture.md` does not exist — the remote repository only has `spec/PAEOS-9-runtime-bootstrap.md` or `spec/PAEOS-9A-runtime-bootstrap.md`. `spec/PAEOS-9-execution-architecture.md` exists only as uncommitted working-tree state in local checkouts.

## 2. Risk & Impact

Any reader cloning `origin/main` cleanly cannot resolve the primary specification citations in `SAEOS-1`, breaking full traceability (A-09 / K4§14).

## 3. Remediation Strategy

- Founder action required: Commit and push `spec/PAEOS-9-execution-architecture.md` to `origin/main`, or update `SAEOS-1` traceability pointers to reference `spec/PAEOS-9A-runtime-bootstrap.md`.
